11	 * (retail-react-app 10.0.0), converted to TypeScript per AGENTS.md's copy-first rule.
12	 *
13	 * The differences from the base file are the TypeScript annotations below and house
14	 * formatting — no changed JSX, hook calls, prop names, or reordered `useEffect`s, and the base
15	 * file's own dead check (`recommendations.length < 1` on what is always an object) is ported
16	 * byte-identical in behaviour. The annotations: a `RecommendedProductsProps` type replacing the
17	 * `propTypes` block; a narrow local `RecommendedProduct` type for the one field read off a
18	 * recommendation-context product (reused for the `productTileProps` callback's own `product`
19	 * param below, since it is that same recommendation-context product); an explicit `boolean`
20	 * param on the one nested callback that isn't contextually typed; and inline
21	 * `{ productId?: string }` / `{ id?: string }` object-type-literal params on four
22	 * `.find`/`.some`/`.map` callbacks whose containing expression is untyped (`any`) and therefore
23	 * supplies no contextual parameter type — `noImplicitAny` flags these regardless of the `any`
24	 * receiver (confirmed against `npx tsc --noEmit`, which is why these four are annotated despite
25	 * this file's own initial plan expecting two of them not to need it). The `{ productId?: string
26	 * }` shape and inline-annotation style mirrors the existing precedent at
27	 * product-detail/index.tsx:437 and :735; the `{ id?: string }` shape matches the field the base
28	 * hook itself reads, `use-einstein.js`'s own `reco.recs?.map((rec) => rec.id)` (line 466).
29	 *
30	 * A sixth adjustment, found by lint rather than tsc: the base file destructures `formatMessage`
31	 * straight off `useIntl()`, but `@typescript-eslint/unbound-method` flags any destructured
32	 * reference to it — `formatMessage` is declared with method-shorthand syntax in
33	 * `@formatjs/intl/src/types.d.ts:64-65`, which this rule always flags regardless of whether the
34	 * real implementation needs `this`. Fix: keep the whole object (`const intl = useIntl();`) and
35	 * call `intl.formatMessage(...)` at each of its five call sites instead of destructuring — a
36	 * property-access call sidesteps the rule entirely, with zero behavioural change. Same
37	 * "toolchain requires a different access shape than the untyped base file used" reasoning as the
38	 * annotations above.
39	 *
40	 * SFCC-83/84 build plan step A6 (2026-09-07) adds one branch: when `recommender ===
41	 * EINSTEIN_RECOMMENDERS.PDP_RECENTLY_VIEWED` (`'viewed-recently-einstein'`, the same string
42	 * `CART_RECENTLY_VIEWED` resolves to — confirmed identical in
43	 * node_modules/@salesforce/retail-react-app/app/constants.js:154-160), `recommendations.recs`
44	 * maps through `selectRecentlyViewedCard` (overrides/app/utils/recentlyViewedCard.ts) and renders
45	 * `ZimmRecentlyViewedRail` instead, gated by `useRecentlyViewedGate`
46	 * (overrides/app/hooks/useRecentlyViewedGate.ts). Every other recommender keeps the original
47	 * `ProductScroller` branch below, untouched.
48	 *
49	 * `ref` is still attached on the Recently Viewed branch too, via a plain wrapping `<Box
50	 * ref={ref}>` — `isOnScreen` below (the impression-tracking gate for `sendViewReco`/
51	 * `dataCloud.sendViewRecommendations`) only works once `ref.current` is a real DOM node
52	 * (use-intersection-observer.js: `if (!ref?.current) return`, with no dependency on which
53	 * component produced that node), and `ZimmRecentlyViewedRail` is a plain function component with
54	 * no `forwardRef` support of its own. Wrapping here, rather than adding `forwardRef` to that
55	 * already-committed component (A5), keeps this fix entirely inside this file.
56	 *
57	 * `headingLevel`/`variation` are added here, not by the mapper: `selectRecentlyViewedCard`'s own
58	 * docblock states both are deliberately excluded from its output because they are this
59	 * container's decision to make. `headingLevel: 'h3'` is inert for this variation —
60	 * `ZimmProductCardContent` never mounts when `variation: 'recentlyViewed'`
61	 * (zimmProductCard/index.tsx's `VARIATION_CONFIG.showContent`) — and matches the one other
62	 * established value for this same required field (product-list/productListCardMapper.ts).
63	 *
64	 * `{...props}` is forwarded to the `<Box>` wrapper (cast to `BoxProps` — this file's own index
65	 * signature types `props` as `Record<string, unknown>`, not safely spreadable onto `Box`'s typed
66	 * props otherwise), matching the ProductScroller branch below exactly. This matters concretely:
67	 * PDP passes `mx={{base: -4, md: -8, lg: 0}}` and Cart passes `mx={{base: -4, sm: -6, lg: 0}}` to
68	 * bleed this component edge-to-edge on mobile/tablet — without forwarding it, this branch would
69	 * render inset inside the page's normal content padding while every sibling rail on the same page
70	 * bleeds to the edge, and `zimmRecentlyViewedRail.css.ts`'s own card-width math (e.g. 201x2=402)
71	 * assumes the full viewport width is actually available. Still worth a live look on PDP/Cart —
72	 * this closes the gap structurally but wasn't visually confirmed in a running browser.
73	 */
